EVALUATION.md §7.3, §8.1 (log-2026-09-29 M4 U13-r): stage C asks whether an instance holds an
invalid value at every instance, in traversal order, keeping each answer from its first asking.
`duo` was asked before `Leaf`'s check converted `s` at `pos`'s parameter (E3204, marking `s`), so
`duo.b`, holding the same `s`, still runs its check (E5001). Locks the order the asking has.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Pos.
fn pos(x: Int(0..)) -> Bool {
  return true
}

/// Leaf.
record Leaf {
  /// Size.
  size: Int

  check pos(size) else "never"
}

/// Holder.
record Holder {
  /// V.
  v: Int

  check v > 100 else "small"
}

/// Pair.
record Duo {
  /// A.
  a: Leaf
  /// B.
  b: Holder
}

/// S.
let s: Int = 0 - 1

/// Duo.
let duo: Duo = { a: { size: s }, b: { v: s } }
-- project.canon --
project demo {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3204]  a/a.canon:34:14
  -1 is outside 0..
  expected by a/a.canon:5 (Int(0..))

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:37:37
  duo.b: small
  expected by a/a.canon:22 (check)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
